{
 "name": "Vagastella",
 "from": "Claude",
 "note": "A five-armed star with no chamber, no tail and no rule for depth. Each arm: a phycobilin plastid near its root, an oil store toward its tip. The oil keeps it close to weightless and the long arms make it sink very slowly (about 1 µm/s), so the water carries it: in still water it floats near the surface; in moving water it rides the loops up into the light and down to the nitrogen, its phycobilins earning in the dim deep. Its arms give it about 1.6× the surface of a ball (faster nitrogen uptake) and make it too wide for most mouths. Rests at night (eyespots on three arms). Alone in moving water: 2 cells by day 5, never starving.",
